.TH mnnn-spaces-run 1  "mnnn-spaces-run 2.22.3" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-spaces\-run \- Run a space (its main), over SOURCE if given
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn spaces run\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR] [\fB\-\-connector\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-pipeline\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-ruleset\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-option\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISPACE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a space (its main), over SOURCE if given
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<ROWS>\fR [default: 20]

.TP
\fB\-\-connector\-dry\-run\fR
Run an ingest\-connector space with a made\-up context: store_raw, pipe and run_ruleset are recorded and listed, not done (fetch is real)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
The context\*(Aqs source name (default: the space\*(Aqs name)
.TP
\fB\-\-pipeline\fR \fI<PIPELINE>\fR
The context\*(Aqs pipeline name
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ruleset\fR \fI<RULESET>\fR
The context\*(Aqs rule set id
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-option\fR \fI<OPTIONS>\fR
A schedule option KEY=VALUE (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR
A starting state value KEY=JSON (repeatable; non\-JSON is text)
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISPACE\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.22.3
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
